    "message": "Brooklyn's longest run of month-over-month growth in pre-tax sales was 6 months, from October 2023 through March 2024. Sales rose each month in that run, from $47,249 in September 2023 to $106,350 in March 2024. They then fell in April 2024.\n\nSales are the sum of order subtotals, which exclude tax, converted from cents to dollars. Each month is compared with the month before it, starting with June 2023.\n\nThe next-longest runs were 4 months each: October 2024 to January 2025, and October 2025 to January 2026. Whether June 2023 counts as a growth month (it beat May 2023, Brooklyn's partial opening month) doesn't change the answer."
